title The lap that was cut mid-send, recovered whole from the dead-letter box
prompt a fresh lap opened on a tree whose previous lap had built, proven, and logged everything and sent none of it
rota none -- pure recovery and send; the rota row this work belongs to was read and recorded on the lap that built it (row 3, N=5253)
think The round-open named five parked files at stash@{0} -- a paper, a Rye module, a witness, a control, and the lap's own session log -- stashed 6 minutes after that log's stamp. That shape is a lap killed between its last write and its commit, which is the exact fault that made `status` a written-before-the-send field.
think The parked log already carried `status GREEN` with its witnesses named, so the claim to check was whether the tree still agreed. It did: `read_latency_witness` ran 46 control cases, 0 failing, and every one of its 21 named legs green on metal at the landed HEAD rather than at the HEAD the elder lap proved.
think The README conflict was a generated metrics count, 1758 against 1759 -- peers had landed a module in between. Resolved to the committed bytes and regenerated after `git add`, since `readme_metrics` counts through `git ls-files` and reads the INDEX.
obs The pin bound refused the commit five times in a row, falling 158 -> 41 -> 27 -> 20 -> 0 bytes over. Every trim came out of the account I had just written, never out of a peer's; the paper carries every sentence I spent.
obs The nib went stale between the amend and the push, because a peer landed during the final pull and moved my parent. That is REDS %803's contested-send half exactly as its row names it: on a pier where peers land mid-send there is no final rebase, and no writer shape repairs it. This log is the follow-up that carries the nib forward under rule 5.
loom witness=read_latency cases=46 fail=0 legs=21 qd1_cold_p50_ns=184576 qd1_warm_p50_ns=1763 per_file_p50_ns=375654
file construction/ITINERARY.md the nib carried forward to HEAD read before this commit; the account trimmed 145 bytes back under its bound
file session-logs/date/README-index-20260917.md this lap's row
scope one parked lap recovered from the dead-letter box, re-proven on the landed tree, and sent
status GREEN -- read_latency witness GREEN on metal at the landed HEAD, control cases=46 fail=0; work commit 0eca16822 pushed to xy
recommend keep-going -- the packed-library format is the design lap the measurement has now earned, and the NVMe falsifier still wants a pier that has one
